{"abstract":[{"text":"An edge colouring with at most Δ + 1 colours (Vizing’s bound), by Misra and Gries’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"constructive proof. Edges in position order, each coloured through a fan at its end with the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"lesser vertex index, every choice the least colour or vertex available. At least Δ colours","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"always, and Δ + 1 on class-2 graphs (odd cycles, odd complete graphs, Petersen), but","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sometimes Δ + 1 on class-1 graphs too (K(4)); on a bipartite graph ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bipartiteEdgeColoring()"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"always gives Δ. O(m · (Δ² + n)) time: a fan has at most Δ vertices, each found among the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"edges at u, and a path at most n edges. O(n + m) memory. For a multigraph","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"digraph.undirectedView"},{"text":" with an antiparallel pair is one), use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"greedyEdgeColoring()"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/edgeColoring()"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/edgecoloring()"]}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"remoteSource":{"fileName":"EdgeColoring.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/ColoringModule\/EdgeCol